export const helpCategories = [{"id":"getting-started","label":"Getting Started","labelHa":"Farawa","order":1},{"id":"everyday","label":"Everyday tasks","labelHa":"Ayyukan yau da kullum","order":2},{"id":"operations","label":"Operations","labelHa":"Ayyuka","order":3},{"id":"configuration","label":"Configuration","labelHa":"Saiti","order":4},{"id":"insights","label":"Insights & tools","labelHa":"Bayanai da kayan aiki","order":5},{"id":"troubleshooting","label":"Troubleshooting","labelHa":"Warware matsaloli","order":6}]
export const helpGuides = [{"slug":"admin-overview","title":"Getting started with the admin dashboard","summary":"Log in, read the dashboard, and find your way around every section.","category":"getting-started","order":1,"keywords":["admin","overview","dashboard","login","log in","first time","new admin","admin home","navigation","navigate","sidebar","stats","numbers","getting started","control room"],"body":"# Getting started with the admin dashboard\n\nThe iPrime admin dashboard is your control room for the whole platform —\nmerchants, riders, orders, money, and support. This guide orients you so you\nknow where everything lives.\n\n---\n\n## Logging in\n\nGo to the admin URL and sign in with your **email** and **password** on the\n**iPrime Admin** screen. If you forget your password, contact another admin to\nreset it.\n\n---\n\n## The Dashboard\n\nThe home **Dashboard** gives you the platform at a glance:\n\n![The admin dashboard](/help/screenshots/admin/dashboard.png)\n\n- **Six headline numbers** — Total Requests, Active Requests, Total Revenue,\n  Merchants, Riders, and Users.\n- **Revenue Trends** and **Request Trends** charts.\n- Quick action panels: **Pending Merchants**, **Failed Transactions**, and\n  **Pending Riders** — each with a **View All** link to jump straight to the\n  full screen.\n\n> 💡 Start your shift here. The pending panels tell you what needs attention\n> right now (merchants and riders waiting for approval, payments that failed).\n\n---\n\n## Finding your way around\n\nEverything is in the left sidebar, grouped by what you do:\n\n| Section | What it's for |\n|---|---|\n| **Dashboard** | The overview above |\n| **Requests** | Live and past delivery orders |\n| **Merchants** | Approve and manage shops |\n| **Categories** | The merchant category list |\n| **Riders** | Approve and manage riders |\n| **Analytics** | Platform-wide reports |\n| **Financial** | Reconciliation and money operations |\n| **Disputes** | Customer/merchant order disputes |\n| **Support** | Support tickets |\n| **Marketing** | Banners and campaigns |\n| **Waitlist** | Pre-launch sign-ups |\n| **Safety** | Safety & compliance |\n| **VTU Plans / Networks** | Airtime, data, cable, electricity pricing |\n| **Customers** | All customer accounts |\n| **Audit Logs** | A record of every admin action |\n| **Transactions** | Every money movement |\n| **Settings** | Platform-wide configuration |\n\nAt the **bottom of the sidebar** you'll find your name, a **light/dark toggle**,\nand **Logout**.\n\n> ⚠️ Admin actions are powerful and **logged**. Approving, suspending, refunding,\n> and changing settings all affect real merchants, riders, and money — and every\n> action is recorded in **Audit Logs**.\n\n---\n\n**Next:** [Approving & managing merchants](/help/admin/managing-merchants) ·\n[Managing riders](/help/admin/managing-riders)\n"},{"slug":"managing-merchants","title":"Approving and managing merchants","summary":"Review applications, approve/reject/suspend, set commission, and approve withdrawals.","category":"operations","order":1,"keywords":["merchants","vendor","store","shop","approve","approve merchant","reject","suspend","block merchant","ban vendor","pending review","application","merchant approval","commission","set commission","withdrawal hold","tags","merchant withdrawals","merchant management"],"body":"# Approving and managing merchants\n\nThe **Merchants** page (titled *Merchant Management*) is where you review new shop\napplications and manage every merchant on the platform.\n\n![Merchant management](/help/screenshots/admin/merchants.png)\n\nFour tabs run across the top:\n\n- **All Merchants** — every shop, searchable\n- **Pending Review** — applications waiting for approval\n- **Withdrawals** — merchant payout requests to approve\n- **Tags & Categories** — manage the tags used for search\n\nThe stat cards (Total Merchants, Pending Review, Active, Pending Withdrawals) are\nclickable shortcuts.\n\n---\n\n## Approve (or reject) a new merchant\n\n1. Open the **Pending Review** tab (or click the *Pending Review* stat card).\n2. Click the merchant to open its application — check the business details,\n   contact, location, and bank account.\n3. Click **\"Approve Application\"** to activate them (a welcome email is sent), or\n   **\"Reject\"** and enter a clear reason explaining what they need to fix.\n\n> ⚠️ Once approved, a merchant becomes visible to customers. Verify the bank\n> account and location look legitimate before approving.\n\n---\n\n## Manage an existing merchant\n\nFrom **All Merchants**, click any shop to open its detail drawer. It has four\ntabs:\n\n- **Profile** — edit business info, location, and hours; toggle admin visibility;\n  **Suspend** / **Unsuspend** the merchant (with a reason).\n- **Commission** — set this merchant's commission rate and see the full change\n  history.\n- **Wallet** — view available/pending balances, the linked bank account, and\n  place or release a **withdrawal hold** (pauses payouts without suspending the\n  shop).\n- **Tags** — assign tags that power search and filtering in the customer app.\n\n> 💡 Use a **withdrawal hold** (Wallet tab) instead of a full suspension when you\n> only need to pause payouts while you investigate — the shop keeps operating.\n\n---\n\n## Approve merchant withdrawals\n\nOpen the **Withdrawals** tab to see payout requests. Approve them individually\nwith the green check, or tick several and use **bulk approve**. Rejecting a\nwithdrawal returns the funds to the merchant's wallet.\n\n> ⚠️ Withdrawals move real money to a bank account — confirm the request looks\n> right before approving.\n\n---\n\n**Next:** [Managing riders](/help/admin/managing-riders) ·\n[Finances & transactions](/help/admin/finance)\n"},{"slug":"managing-riders","title":"Managing riders","summary":"Approve rider applications, review documents, and watch for expiry.","category":"operations","order":2,"keywords":["riders","driver","delivery driver","approve","approve rider","reject","suspend","block rider","deactivate rider","documents","papers","verify documents","licence","license","insurance","expiry","expired documents","online","availability","pending approvals","earnings"],"body":"# Managing riders\n\nThe **Riders** page (*Riders Management*) is where you approve rider applications,\nkeep an eye on who's active, and act on documents that are expiring.\n\n![Riders management](/help/screenshots/admin/riders.png)\n\nTwo tabs: **All Riders** and **Pending Approvals**. The stat cards show **Total\nRiders** (and how many are online now), **Active**, **Pending Review**, and\n**Suspended**.\n\nEach rider shows a **status** — *Pending*, *Active*, *Suspended*, or *Rejected* —\nand, for active riders, an availability badge: *Online*, *On delivery*, or\n*Offline*.\n\n---\n\n## Approve a new rider\n\n1. Open **Pending Approvals** (or the *Pending Review* stat card).\n2. Click a rider to open their detail drawer and review the **Documents** tab —\n   ID, licence, vehicle registration, and insurance.\n3. **Approve** the rider, or **Reject** them with a reason.\n\n> ⚠️ Check that documents are valid and not expired before approving — riders\n> handle customers' orders and cash.\n\n---\n\n## A rider's detail drawer\n\nClick any rider to open their drawer, which has three tabs:\n\n- **Profile** — personal and vehicle details; **Suspend** (with a reason that\n  tells them what's needed to lift it).\n- **Documents** — uploaded ID/licence/insurance with their **expiry dates**.\n- **Earnings** — what the rider has made.\n\n---\n\n## Watch for expiring documents\n\nRiders' documents (licence, insurance, etc.) have expiry dates. The system flags\ndocuments that are **expired** or **expiring soon** so you can ask the rider to\nre-upload before it becomes a problem.\n\n> 💡 Use the search box to find a rider quickly by **name or phone**.\n\n---\n\n**Next:** [Monitoring delivery requests](/help/admin/delivery-requests) ·\n[Resolving disputes](/help/admin/resolving-disputes)\n"},{"slug":"delivery-requests","title":"Monitoring delivery requests","summary":"Track every order, look into the details, and cancel when necessary.","category":"operations","order":3,"keywords":["requests","orders","delivery","deliveries","order details","view order","status","cancel","cancel delivery","stop delivery","track","track orders","live orders","customer","rider","merchant","monitor"],"body":"# Monitoring delivery requests\n\nThe **Requests** page is the live and historical record of every delivery order\non the platform — food, groceries, pharmacy, and packages.\n\n![Delivery requests](/help/screenshots/admin/requests.png)\n\n---\n\n## What you'll see\n\nEach request shows its **customer**, **merchant** (if any), **status**, **total**,\nand **time**. An order moves through these stages:\n\n**Requested → Accepted → Processing → Ready for Pickup → Rider Assigned → Picked\nup → In transit → Delivered** (or **Cancelled**).\n\nUse the **search box** to find an order by **customer name or phone**, and filter\nby status to focus on, say, only active or only cancelled orders.\n\n---\n\n## Look into an order\n\nClick a request to see the full picture — items, the customer and merchant,\ndelivery address, the assigned rider, and the money split (subtotal, delivery\nfee, platform fee).\n\n> 💡 When a customer or merchant contacts support about an order, find it here\n> first — it shows exactly where the order is and who's involved.\n\n---\n\n## Cancel an order\n\nIf an order is stuck or needs intervention, you can **cancel** it. You'll be\nasked for a **cancellation reason** — this is recorded and may trigger a refund\nto the customer.\n\n> ⚠️ Cancelling can refund the customer and affects the merchant and rider.\n> Only do it when an order genuinely can't be completed, and always give a clear\n> reason.\n\n---\n\n**Next:** [Resolving disputes](/help/admin/resolving-disputes) ·\n[Finances & transactions](/help/admin/finance)\n"},{"slug":"resolving-disputes","title":"Resolving disputes","summary":"Investigate order disputes and decide refunds fairly.","category":"operations","order":4,"keywords":["disputes","dispute","refund","approve refund","give refund","money back","full refund","partial refund","reject dispute","resolution","resolve dispute","complaint","customer complaint","investigate","evidence","order issue","order disputes"],"body":"# Resolving disputes\n\nWhen a customer or merchant disputes an order, it lands on the **Disputes** page\n(*Order Disputes*). This is where you investigate and decide the outcome fairly.\n\n![Order disputes](/help/screenshots/admin/disputes.png)\n\n---\n\n## Review a dispute\n\n1. On the **Disputes** list, click a dispute to open it.\n2. Read the history — the customer's claim, the merchant's response, and any\n   attached evidence (photos, notes).\n3. Use the reply box to **reply to the customer, the merchant, or leave an\n   internal note** (notes are for admins only and aren't shown to either party).\n\n> 💡 Gather both sides before deciding. The order's GPS log, proof-of-delivery\n> photo, and timestamps (on the **Requests** page) are your best evidence.\n\n---\n\n## Decide the outcome\n\nWhen you're ready to resolve, choose one of:\n\n| Outcome | What it does |\n|---|---|\n| **Full refund** | Refund the customer the full amount |\n| **Partial refund** | Refund part of the amount |\n| **Resolved (no refund)** | Close it in the merchant's/rider's favour |\n| **Reject dispute** | Dismiss the dispute |\n\nAdd **resolution notes** (these are shown to the customer) explaining the\ndecision, then confirm.\n\n> ⚠️ Refunds move real money. Make sure the evidence supports the outcome before\n> you confirm — the decision is final and recorded in **Audit Logs**.\n\n---\n\n**Next:** [Handling support tickets](/help/admin/support-tickets) ·\n[Managing customers](/help/admin/managing-customers)\n"},{"slug":"support-tickets","title":"Handling support tickets","summary":"Pick up tickets, assign yourself, reply, and move them to resolution.","category":"operations","order":5,"keywords":["support","tickets","support ticket","assign","assign to me","status","open","in progress","resolved","closed","reply","respond","complaint","customer complaints","customer issues","customer service","help requests"],"body":"# Handling support tickets\n\nThe **Support** page (*Support Tickets*) is where customer and merchant help\nrequests come in. This guide covers picking up a ticket and working it to\nresolution.\n\n![Support tickets](/help/screenshots/admin/support.png)\n\n---\n\n## Work a ticket\n\n1. On the **Support Tickets** list, click a ticket to open it. Use **Refresh** to\n   pull in new ones.\n2. The detail view shows the **Customer**, the **Assignment**, and the **Status**.\n3. Click **\"Assign to me\"** so the team knows you're handling it.\n4. Reply to the customer in the conversation, and update the **Status** as you go:\n   - **Open** → just arrived\n   - **In Progress** → you're working it\n   - **Pending User** → waiting on the customer to reply\n   - **Resolved** / **Closed** → done\n\n> 💡 Always **assign yourself** before replying so two admins don't work the same\n> ticket. Set it to **Pending User** when the ball is in the customer's court so\n> it doesn't look unattended.\n\n---\n\n## Tips\n\n- Keep replies clear and friendly — the customer sees them.\n- Use an **internal note** (where available) for context you don't want the\n  customer to see.\n- If a ticket is really about an order dispute or a refund, handle the money side\n  under [Disputes](/help/admin/resolving-disputes) or\n  [Finances](/help/admin/finance) and link it in your reply.\n\n---\n\n**Next:** [Managing customers](/help/admin/managing-customers) ·\n[Resolving disputes](/help/admin/resolving-disputes)\n"},{"slug":"managing-customers","title":"Managing customers","summary":"Look up customers, review their history, and suspend or adjust where needed.","category":"operations","order":6,"keywords":["customers","customer","user","find customer","look up","search customers","suspend","ban","ban user","block customer","freeze account","deactivate customer","wallet adjustment","wallet balance","order history","addresses","account"],"body":"# Managing customers\n\nThe **Customers** page lists every customer account on the platform. Use it to\nlook up a customer, review their history, and take action when needed.\n\n![Customers](/help/screenshots/admin/customers.png)\n\n---\n\n## Find a customer\n\nUse the **search box** to find someone by **name, email, or phone**.\n\n## Open a customer's profile\n\nClick a customer to open their detail page, which has three tabs:\n\n- **Requests** — every order they've placed\n- **Transactions** — their wallet and payment history\n- **Addresses** — their saved delivery addresses\n\nThis is the fastest way to verify a complaint — you can see exactly what they\nordered and what they were charged.\n\n---\n\n## Actions you can take\n\n- **Suspend** an account (you'll enter a reason) if it's being abused, and\n  unsuspend it later.\n- **Adjust their wallet** where allowed — you'll be asked *\"Why is this change\n  being made?\"*. Always give a clear reason; it's recorded.\n\n> ⚠️ Wallet adjustments and suspensions are sensitive, real-money/real-account\n> actions. Double-check you have the right customer, and always record the\n> reason — it shows up in **Audit Logs**.\n\n---\n\n**Next:** [Finances & transactions](/help/admin/finance) ·\n[Resolving disputes](/help/admin/resolving-disputes)\n"},{"slug":"finance","title":"Finances, transactions & withdrawals","summary":"Read the transaction ledger, run financial operations, and approve payouts.","category":"operations","order":7,"keywords":["finance","transactions","transaction history","view transactions","ledger","payment","refund","commission","withdrawal","approve withdrawal","approve payout","payout","cash out","send money","pay merchant","pay rider","reconciliation","escrow","failed transaction","financial operations","money"],"body":"# Finances, transactions & withdrawals\n\nMoney on the platform is managed across three places: **Transactions** (the\nledger), **Financial** (operations and reconciliation), and the **Withdrawals**\ntab on the Merchants page (payouts).\n\n---\n\n## Transactions\n\nThe **Transactions** page is the complete record of every money movement.\n\n![Transactions](/help/screenshots/admin/transactions.png)\n\nFilter by **type** — *Payment*, *Refund*, *Delivery Earning*, *Commission*,\n*Withdrawal* — and by **status** — *Pending*, *Completed*, *Failed*.\n\n> 💡 Chasing a customer's \"my money didn't arrive\" report? Filter to their\n> transaction type and status here to see exactly what happened.\n\n---\n\n## Financial operations\n\nThe **Financial** page (*Financial Operations*) is for platform-level money\nmanagement — reconciliation, escrow, and the system wallets that hold funds in\ntransit between customers, merchants, and riders.\n\n> ⚠️ Actions here affect platform-wide balances. Make sure you understand a\n> figure before acting on it, and use the **Transactions** ledger to back up any\n> investigation.\n\n---\n\n## Approving withdrawals\n\nMerchant payout requests are approved on the **Merchants → Withdrawals** tab — see\n[Approving & managing merchants](/help/admin/managing-merchants#approve-merchant-withdrawals).\nYou can approve them one at a time or in bulk; rejecting one returns the funds to\nthe merchant's wallet.\n\n---\n\n## Failed transactions\n\nThe **Dashboard** highlights recent **Failed Transactions**. Open one from there\nor from the Transactions page to investigate — a failed payment may need a retry\nor a refund.\n\n---\n\n**Next:** [Managing customers](/help/admin/managing-customers) ·\n[Categories, VTU networks & plans](/help/admin/catalogue)\n"},{"slug":"catalogue","title":"Categories, VTU networks & plans","summary":"Manage merchant categories and the airtime/data/cable/electricity catalogue.","category":"configuration","order":1,"keywords":["categories","merchant categories","add category","vtu","networks","plans","pricing","airtime","data","data plan","cable","cable tv","electricity","biller","provider id","network provider","change price","icon"],"body":"# Categories, VTU networks & plans\n\nThese three screens control what merchants can sell under and what bills\ncustomers can pay — the platform's catalogue and pricing.\n\n---\n\n## Merchant categories\n\nThe **Categories** page (*Merchant Categories*) is the master list of categories a\nmerchant can belong to — Food, Groceries, Pharmacy, Fashion, and so on.\n\n![Merchant categories](/help/screenshots/admin/categories.png)\n\nCreate or edit a category with a **name**, **description**, **icon** (pick from\nthe icon list), and colour. Categories also carry an *attribute schema* that\ntells the merchant product form which options (size, colour, pack units) to show.\n\n> ⚠️ Changing or removing a category affects every merchant in it and how their\n> products are shown to customers. Edit with care.\n\n---\n\n## VTU networks\n\nThe **VTU Networks** page maps the airtime/data/cable/electricity providers to the\nIDs our VTU partner uses. You manage these by type so you can update a provider ID\nwithout a code change.\n\n![VTU networks](/help/screenshots/admin/vtu-networks.png)\n\n---\n\n## VTU plans & pricing\n\nThe **VTU Plans** page (*VTU Pricing*) is where you manage the actual sellable\nitems — data bundles, cable packages, and the cost/selling price for each.\n\n![VTU pricing](/help/screenshots/admin/vtu-plans.png)\n\nUse the tabs to switch between **Airtime, Data, Cable, and Electricity**, and add\nor edit a plan's name, validity, and price.\n\n> 💡 Selling price vs cost price sets your margin on each bundle. Keep these in\n> sync with your VTU provider's current rates so you never sell at a loss.\n\n---\n\n**Next:** [Marketing & platform settings](/help/admin/marketing-settings) ·\n[Analytics, safety & tools](/help/admin/analytics-tools)\n"},{"slug":"marketing-settings","title":"Marketing & platform settings","summary":"Manage banners, and configure platform-wide fees, commission, and notifications.","category":"configuration","order":2,"keywords":["marketing","banners","banner","promo","campaigns","settings","platform configuration","commission","commission rate","commission percentage","service charge","fees","platform fees","delivery fee","limits","notification settings"],"body":"# Marketing & platform settings\n\nTwo screens for shaping the platform: **Marketing** (what customers see) and\n**Settings** (how the platform behaves).\n\n---\n\n## Marketing\n\nThe **Marketing** page (*Marketing Oversight*) is where you manage the banners and\npromotional content shown to customers in the app.\n\n![Marketing oversight](/help/screenshots/admin/marketing.png)\n\nCreate, edit, schedule, and remove banners. Keep them current — expired or\nbroken promos are the first thing customers notice.\n\n---\n\n## Platform settings\n\nThe **Settings** page controls platform-wide behaviour, in three sections:\n\n![Platform settings](/help/screenshots/admin/settings.png)\n\n- **Platform Configuration** — core fees and rules (delivery fares, withdrawal\n  limits and fees, minimums, and similar).\n- **Commission Defaults** — the default commission rate applied to new merchants\n  (individual merchants can be overridden on their Merchant → Commission tab).\n- **Notification Settings** — which alerts the platform sends, e.g. **New Order\n  Alerts**.\n\n> ⚠️ Settings here affect **everyone** — every order, payout, and merchant. Change\n> one value at a time, and note what you changed and why. Everything is recorded\n> in **Audit Logs**.\n\n> 💡 Your own admin account details (name, password) are under **Profile**, not\n> here.\n\n---\n\n**Next:** [Analytics, safety & tools](/help/admin/analytics-tools) ·\n[Categories & VTU](/help/admin/catalogue)\n"},{"slug":"analytics-tools","title":"Analytics, safety, waitlist & audit logs","summary":"Reports, safety signals, the pre-launch waitlist, and the record of every admin action.","category":"insights","order":1,"keywords":["analytics","reports","revenue","orders report","geographic","safety","compliance","waitlist","pre-launch","signups","sign ups","audit logs","audit trail","history","who changed","who deleted","track changes","admin activity","activity history","who made a change"],"body":"# Analytics, safety, waitlist & audit logs\n\nThe remaining admin screens for insight and oversight.\n\n---\n\n## Analytics\n\nThe **Analytics** page (*Platform Analytics*) is your reporting hub, organised\ninto tabs:\n\n![Platform analytics](/help/screenshots/admin/analytics.png)\n\n- **Overview** — the headline numbers\n- **Revenue** — money trends over time\n- **Orders** — order volumes and patterns\n- **Customers** — growth and behaviour\n- **Geographic** — where activity is happening\n\n> 💡 Use the date ranges to compare periods. A single merchant's analytics is\n> available from that merchant's drawer on the **Merchants** page.\n\n---\n\n## Safety & compliance\n\nThe **Safety** page (*Safety & Compliance*) surfaces safety- and compliance-\nrelated signals across riders and deliveries so issues can be caught early.\n\n![Safety & compliance](/help/screenshots/admin/safety.png)\n\n---\n\n## Pre-launch waitlist\n\nThe **Waitlist** page (*Pre-launch Waitlist*) lists everyone who signed up before\nlaunch — customers, riders, and merchants. Use **Refresh** to pull the latest,\nand export the list when you're ready to reach out.\n\n![Pre-launch waitlist](/help/screenshots/admin/waitlist.png)\n\n---\n\n## Audit logs\n\nThe **Audit Logs** page is the platform's memory — a record of **every admin\naction**: approvals, suspensions, refunds, settings changes, and more.\n\n![Audit logs](/help/screenshots/admin/audit-logs.png)\n\n**Filter by action** to trace what happened, when, and who did it.\n\n> 💡 If something looks wrong — an unexpected refund, a merchant suddenly\n> suspended — the Audit Logs tell you exactly which admin did it and when. It's\n> your first stop for any \"who changed this?\" question.\n\n---\n\n**Next:** [Back to the admin overview](/help/admin/admin-overview)\n"}]
